Z||000000||wallybowman||12-04-2000||12:28 AM||||I have found a 1984 2M4 for $100.00 that is<BR>an automatic that I would like to swap to a<BR>manual. Just about what does this swap cost<BR>and how much work is it? Since I work on cars<BR>for a living the labor will be no problem.<BR>The owner installed sidedraft Webers on the<BR>car and that's the main reason I'm getting the car. Thanks to all for any info.  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||12-04-2000||12:31 AM||||Not too bad. Add the clutch pedal, swap the brake pedal (smaller), master cylinder, new axles (different size), shifter/cables, flywheel, prom (for a manual trans. Use the same ECM). Find a manual trans donor car in a wrecking yard.<P><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hank is Here||12-04-2000||12:36 AM||||The owner installed sidedraft Webers on the car and that's the main reason I'm getting the car. Thanks to all for any info.  <P>Sidedraft.......eugh, darn British. I didn't know anyone in North America actually like those darn things<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I am not making any generalizations  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||12-04-2000||01:03 AM||||Side drafts are nice. Why he did it is beyond me though. That means he dumped the ECM. Oh well.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||12-04-2000||01:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>Not too bad. Add the clutch pedal, swap the brake pedal (smaller), master cylinder, new axles (different size), shifter/cables, flywheel, prom (for a manual trans. Use the same ECM). Find a manual trans donor car in a wrecking yard.<P><BR>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-04-2000).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What's different between the Auto and Stick PROM's? I ran my stick conversion with the Auto PROM and it ran well. It just told the scanner that the TCC was non-existent.||||reg||1
